tablishing that `signed_min|s <=s ~(s-t)|s` and using transitivity.\n\nRather than continuing to chase the logical structure in circles, I think the clearest path forward is to write out the proof directly in Coq and let the case analysis guide me. I'll structure it around a key lemma: if the unsigned value of `a` is at most the unsigned value of `b` minus one, and both have the same sign bit, then `a` is signed-less-than `b`. Then I can apply this with the bound on `~(s-t)` to establish the backward direction.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2582,"cache_read_input_tokens":133856,"output_tokens":1429,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2582,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":1429,"cache_read_input_tokens":133856,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2582,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2582},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CaRU3UnQU91rvWu7wMJUe","type":"assistant","uuid":"b016dfc0-0fb1-4947-b9cd-7314a82637f0","timestamp":"2026-04-26T00:52:26.136Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/hakull245/bitvector-vibe-proving","sessionId":"2b65148c-b4a0-40d0-9fba-835c4508523c","version":"2.1.120","gitBranch":"haVibeProving"}
