t neg = contradiction. 4th bullet = both nonneg = `lia`. Code had them reversed. Fixed by swapping the bullet blocks.\n   - **`HD_last` proof**: `last_map_negb` gives `last(map negb l) false = negb(last l false)`. After `rewrite HV_last in H`, got `H : false = negb (last...)`. Fixed by adding `symmetry in H. rewrite negb_false_iff in H. exact H.`\n   - **`HVs_lt_Ph` proof**: `last_false_list2int_ub` needs `list2int v < pow2_int (length v - 1)` but the lengths didn't match. Fixed by computing length equality explicitly:\n     ```coq\n     { assert (Hlen_Vs : length (map2 orb (map negb (subst_list s t)) s) = length s).\n       { rewrite <- (@map2_or_length (map negb (subst_list s t)) s HLen_V). exact HLen_V. }\n       unfold Vs, Ph. rewrite <- Hlen_Vs.\n       apply last_false_list2int_ub; [exact HVs_ne | exact HVs_sign]. }\n     ```\n   - **`rewrite Hxs_sign, Ht_sign in Hslt` failure** (ONGOING): Error \"Found no subterm matching `last (map2 orb x s) false` in Hslt.\" Attempts:\n     - `rewrite Hxs_sign, Ht_sign in Hslt` → failed\n     - `rewrite HXs_unfold in Hslt` (explicit) → failed with \"bv_or x s not in Hslt\" (confirming `rewrite HXs_unfold in *` had already rewritten Hslt)\n     - `revert Hslt. rewrite Hxs_sign, Ht_sign. simpl. intro Hslt.` → failed (same \"not found\" in goal)\n     - `simp only [Hxs_sign, Ht_sign] in Hslt` → syntax error (simp not standard Coq)\n     - `remember (last (map2 orb x s) false) as bxs eqn:Hxs_sign. destruct bxs.` then `rewrite Ht_sign in Hslt. simpl in Hslt.` → **CURRENT ERROR**: \"Found no subterm matching `last t false` in Hslt\"\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   The central unsolved problem is extracting arithmetic from `Hslt` inside the `(false,true)` contradiction sub-case of `bvor_slt_key`. The hypothesis `Hslt` (after all transformations) should have the form:\n   ```\n   (if last (map2 orb x s) false then list2int (map2 orb x s) - P\n    else list2int (map2 orb x s)) < (if last t false then T - P else T)\n   ```\n   But neither