n.\n\n   - **\"Unable to unify `bv_slt ?M2807 ?M2808 = true` with Z comparison\"** at line 15840:\n     Cause: `apply bv_slt_tf` was in the `-` branch `* last t = false` case, but the outer GOAL had been transformed from `bv_slt ... = true` to a Z arithmetic form `(if last (map2 orb ...) s false then Vs - P else Vs) < T` by the `rewrite bv_slt_iff_sbv2int` + `unfold sbv2int` + `set/fold/rewrite` chain. This code path was never previously reached due to earlier compilation errors.\n     Fix (most recent, not yet compiled): Replace with arithmetic reasoning:\n     ```coq\n     assert (HVs_lt_P : (Vs < P)%Z).\n     { unfold Vs. rewrite HP_eq.\n       apply (@list2int_lt_pow2_int (map2 orb (map negb (subst_list s t)) s) (length s)).\n       exact (eq_trans (@map2_or_length (map negb (subst_list s t)) s HLen_V) HLen_V). }\n     rewrite HVs_neg. simpl. lia.\n     ```\n\n   - **`neg_bv_or` gives `bv_or` form but assertion expected `map2 orb` form** (line 15824):\n     The `apply (@neg_bv_or n x s Hx Hs Hs_sign)` to prove `last (map2 orb x s) false = true` failed because `neg_bv_or` concludes `last (bv_or x s) false = true`, and `bv_or x s ≠ map2 orb x s` definitionally.\n     Fix: Changed assertion to `last (bv_or x s) false = true` and added `rewrite HXs_unfold in Hxs_neg` afterward.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   The central challenge was that `Hslt` (the arithmetic form of `bv_slt (bv_or x s) t = true`) after all the `set/fold/rewrite` transforms had its sign-bit subterms (`last (map2 orb x s) false` and `last t false`) inaccessible to `rewrite`. The solution was to bypass this entirely: save `Hslt_bv` as a copy of `Hslt` before any transformation, then derive fresh `Harith` assertions using `proj1 bv_slt_iff_sbv2int Hslt_bv` followed by `unfold sbv2int` and sign rewrites in the fresh hypothesis (which works because it wasn't touched by set/fold operations).\n\n   A secondary challenge was that the outer GOAL was also transformed from `bv_slt` to Z arithmetic form, so `appl