{"parentUuid":"f4822a14-6eea-45ab-a323-d1aa495d7537","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01YGg9WQfdQwRsvz8jsvfiFZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01J9e32atwz767xkRHzbvM4z","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/home/hakull245/bitvector-vibe-proving/CLAUDE.md","old_string":"## bv_or Proofs — Patterns and Pitfalls\n\n**`bv_or x s` is propositionally, not definitionally, equal to `map2 orb x s`.**\nUnfold it early and save the equation as a hypothesis:\n\n```coq\nassert (HXs_unfold : bv_or x s = map2 orb x s).\n{ unfold bv_or. rewrite Hx, Hs, N.eqb_refl. unfold bits. reflexivity. }\nrewrite HXs_unfold in *.\n```\n\nAfter this, `last`, `length`, and list lemmas apply directly.\n\n**Save hypotheses before `set`/`fold` chains.**\nAfter `rewrite bv_slt_iff_sbv2int ... in Hslt` + `unfold sbv2int` + `set/fold`, sign-bit subterms\n(`last (map2 orb ...) false`) become inaccessible to `rewrite ... in Hslt`.\nFix: copy the hypothesis first:\n\n```coq\npose proof Hslt as Hslt_bv.                      (* save bv_slt form *)\nrewrite (@bv_slt_iff_sbv2int ...) in Hslt.        (* now transform Hslt *)\n```\n\nThen derive arithmetic sub-goals from `Hslt_bv` using `proj1 (bv_slt_iff_sbv2int ...) Hslt_bv`.\n\n**When the goal is already in Z form, don't use `bv_slt_tf`.**\nAfter `rewrite bv_slt_iff_sbv2int` the goal is a Z `<` comparison with `if-then-else` sign branches.\nClose it by rewriting the sign bits (from `eqn:` hypotheses or derived assertions), then `simpl. lia.`:\n\n```coq\nrewrite HVs_pos, Ht_last_false. simpl. lia.\n```\n\n**`proj1`/`proj2` to select iff direction.**\n`apply (bv_slt_iff_sbv2int ...)` fails when the goal is a Z comparison (Coq can't auto-select the\ndirection of an `iff`). Use `proj1`/`proj2` explicitly:\n\n```coq\nexact (proj1 (@bv_slt_iff_sbv2int n a b Ha Hb) H_slt).\n```\n\n**`neg_bv_or` only inspects the second argument's last bit.**\n`neg_bv_or : size x = n -> size s = n -> last s false = true -> last (bv_or x s) false = true`\nWhen the first argument has `last = true` (not the second), use `bv_or_comm` first.\n`bv_or_comm` has implicit `n, a, b` — pass only the two size proofs:\n\n```coq\nrewrite (bv_or_comm HV_sz Hs).    (* swap to put the true-last arg second *)\napply (@neg_bv_or n s v Hs HV_sz). (* now s is second, v has last=true *)\n```\n\n**`map2_or_length` direction.**\n`map2_or_length a b H : length a = length (map2 orb a b)` — the list comes on the right.\nTo prove `length (map2 orb a b) = n` use `eq_sym` + `eq_trans`:\n\n```coq\nexact (eq_trans (eq_sym (@map2_or_length a b H_ab)) H_a).\n```\n\n## Checklist Before Claiming a Proof Done","new_string":"## Proof Tactics — General Pitfalls\n\n**Save hypotheses before `set`/`fold` chains.**\nAfter `rewrite <iff_lemma> in H` + `unfold` + `set/fold`, subterms inside `H` (e.g. sign bits)\nbecome inaccessible to further `rewrite ... in H`. Copy first:\n\n```coq\npose proof H as H_orig.          (* save original form *)\nrewrite (@some_iff ...) in H.    (* now transform H freely *)\n```\n\nThen derive sub-goals from `H_orig` using `proj1`/`proj2`.\n\n**Use `proj1`/`proj2` to select iff direction — never `apply`.**\n`apply (some_iff ...)` fails when the goal or hypothesis is on the wrong side of an `↔`.\nCoq cannot auto-select the direction. Use `proj1`/`proj2` explicitly:\n\n```coq\nexact (proj1 (@bv_slt_iff_sbv2int n a b Ha Hb) H_slt).\n```\n\n**After rewriting a goal to Z form, close with `rewrite sign. simpl. lia.`**\nOnce the goal has been converted (e.g. via `bv_slt_iff_sbv2int` + `unfold sbv2int`) to a Z\ncomparison with `if-then-else` sign branches, tactics like `bv_slt_tf` that expect a `bv_slt = true`\ngoal will fail. Rewrite the sign bits from `eqn:` hypotheses, then `simpl. lia.`:\n\n```coq\nrewrite Hsign_pos, Ht_sign_neg. simpl. lia.\n```\n\n## Checklist Before Claiming a Proof Done"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":56165,"cache_read_input_tokens":10679,"output_tokens":2185,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":56165,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":3,"output_tokens":2185,"cache_read_input_tokens":10679,"cache_creation_input_tokens":56165,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":56165},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":{"cache_miss_reason":{"type":"previous_message_not_found"}}},"requestId":"req_011CaTY6VJxaQmannuj6fFt5","type":"assistant","uuid":"ad0e1850-e9c9-4d6f-859a-b6ff95a1ab23","timestamp":"2026-04-27T03:06:57.773Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/hakull245/bitvector-vibe-proving","sessionId":"2b65148c-b4a0-40d0-9fba-835c4508523c","version":"2.1.120","gitBranch":"haVibeProving","slug":"hazy-chasing-owl"}
