{"parentUuid":"a1695286-3bc6-491f-8634-fa622fdaeecf","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01JZqcPrp3jypEyCPxrKaCDQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants a brief explanation of the three insights added to CLAUDE.md. Let me explain them clearly and concisely.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":210,"cache_read_input_tokens":69068,"output_tokens":481,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":210,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":3,"output_tokens":481,"cache_read_input_tokens":69068,"cache_creation_input_tokens":210,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":210},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CaTYNK9xo2G3fL2FJvBPs","type":"assistant","uuid":"5ac82915-3486-4f0e-b1df-872ab0eba606","timestamp":"2026-04-27T03:09:57.384Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/hakull245/bitvector-vibe-proving","sessionId":"2b65148c-b4a0-40d0-9fba-835c4508523c","version":"2.1.120","gitBranch":"haVibeProving","slug":"hazy-chasing-owl"}
{"parentUuid":"5ac82915-3486-4f0e-b1df-872ab0eba606","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01JZqcPrp3jypEyCPxrKaCDQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**1. Save hyps before `set`/`fold` chains**\n\nWhen you rewrite a hypothesis like `Hslt` from `bv_slt ... = true` into arithmetic form, then run `set (T := list2int t)` etc., Coq replaces occurrences of `list2int t` with `T` — but only those it can syntactically identify. Subterms that were already inside `if`-expressions or deeply nested often get missed, so a later `rewrite last_t_sign in Hslt` fails with \"no subterm matching\". Saving a copy before the chain means you always have the original form to extract facts from.\n\n**2. `proj1`/`proj2` for iff direction**\n\n`apply H` when `H : A ↔ B` only works if the goal is exactly `A` or `B`. If the goal is `B` and you have a proof of `A`, Coq won't automatically pick the forward direction — it just fails. `proj1 H : A → B` and `proj2 H : B → A` make the direction explicit and compose cleanly with function application.\n\n**3. Z-form goal: `rewrite sign. simpl. lia.`**\n\n`bv_slt_iff_sbv2int` rewrites the *goal* from `bv_slt a b = true` into `(sbv2int n a < sbv2int n b)%Z`. After that, tactics like `bv_slt_tf` — which produce `bv_slt = true` as their conclusion — can no longer unify with the goal. The pattern instead is: rewrite the `if last ... then ... - P else ...` sign branches using known `eqn:` hypotheses, let `simpl` reduce the `if true/false`, then let `lia` close the resulting linear inequality."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":210,"cache_read_input_tokens":69068,"output_tokens":481,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":210,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":3,"output_tokens":481,"cache_read_input_tokens":69068,"cache_creation_input_tokens":210,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":210},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CaTYNK9xo2G3fL2FJvBPs","type":"assistant","uuid":"9216ab3f-3a60-4c4b-b94d-343324931b69","timestamp":"2026-04-27T03:10:05.538Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/hakull245/bitvector-vibe-proving","sessionId":"2b65148c-b4a0-40d0-9fba-835c4508523c","version":"2.1.120","gitBranch":"haVibeProving","slug":"hazy-chasing-owl"}
