{"parentUuid":"9216ab3f-3a60-4c4b-b94d-343324931b69","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"536cd876-2d64-434f-ac52-a794be4a5df1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"What are eqn: hypotheses and give me an example for \nWhen you rewrite a hypothesis like Hslt from bv_slt ... = true into arithmetic form, then run set (T := list2int t) etc., Coq replaces occurrences of list2int t with T — but only those it can syntactically identify. Subterms that were already inside if-expressions or deeply nested often get missed, so a later rewrite last_t_sign in Hslt fails with \"no subterm matching\". Saving a copy before the chain means you always have the original form to extract facts from."}]},"uuid":"326d2442-ba7c-492d-8831-674b30f1b267","timestamp":"2026-04-27T03:12:22.070Z","permissionMode":"acceptEdits","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/hakull245/bitvector-vibe-proving","sessionId":"2b65148c-b4a0-40d0-9fba-835c4508523c","version":"2.1.120","gitBranch":"haVibeProving","slug":"hazy-chasing-owl"}
{"type":"file-history-snapshot","messageId":"326d2442-ba7c-492d-8831-674b30f1b267","snapshot":{"messageId":"326d2442-ba7c-492d-8831-674b30f1b267","trackedFileBackups":{"BVList.v":{"backupFileName":"126828487f172d5a@v2","version":2,"backupTime":"2026-04-27T00:52:19.887Z"},"CLAUDE.md":{"backupFileName":"67f5f64815a3bd03@v3","version":3,"backupTime":"2026-04-27T03:09:54.321Z"}},"timestamp":"2026-04-27T03:12:22.093Z"},"isSnapshotUpdate":false}
{"parentUuid":"326d2442-ba7c-492d-8831-674b30f1b267","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_015AEyu17a2TUPdYux1H7sse","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**`eqn:` hypotheses**\n\nWhen you write `destruct (expr) eqn:H`, Coq destructs the value and also adds `H : expr = true` (or `= false`) to the context. Without `eqn:`, you get the case split but no named proof of what the expression equals. Example:\n\n```coq\ndestruct (last t false) eqn:Ht_sign.\n(* true branch: Ht_sign : last t false = true  *)\n(* false branch: Ht_sign : last t false = false *)\n```\n\n---\n\n**Concrete example of the save-before-chain pattern**\n\nSay you have `Hslt : bv_slt (bv_or x s) t = true` and you want to both (a) work in Z arithmetic and (b) eventually case-split on the sign bit of `bv_or x s`.\n\n```coq\npose proof Hslt as Hslt_bv.                              (* copy: still bv_slt form *)\nrewrite (@bv_slt_iff_sbv2int n (bv_or x s) t ...) in Hslt.\nunfold sbv2int in Hslt.\nset (Xs := list2int (map2 orb x s)) in *.\nset (T  := list2int t) in *.\n(* Now Hslt : (if last (map2 orb x s) false then Xs - P else Xs) < ... *)\n```\n\nLater, in the `last (map2 orb x s) false = true` sub-case, you want the arithmetic consequence with the sign bit substituted. But `rewrite Hxs_sign in Hslt` fails — the `set` chain may not have left `last (map2 orb x s) false` as a visible subterm in `Hslt`.\n\nInstead, use the saved copy:\n\n```coq\ndestruct (last (map2 orb x s) false) eqn:Hxs_sign.\n* (* Hxs_sign : last (map2 orb x s) false = true *)\n  assert (Harith : (Xs - P < T - P)%Z).\n  { (* derive from Hslt_bv, which is still bv_slt form *)\n    have H := proj1 (@bv_slt_iff_sbv2int n (map2 orb x s) t ...) Hslt_bv.\n    unfold sbv2int in H. rewrite Hxs_sign, Ht_sign in H. simpl in H. exact H. }\n```\n\nThe fresh `H` is local and untouched by `set`, so `rewrite Hxs_sign in H` succeeds."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":621,"cache_read_input_tokens":69278,"output_tokens":669,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":621,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":3,"output_tokens":669,"cache_read_input_tokens":69278,"cache_creation_input_tokens":621,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":621},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CaTYZE4vwupzsqi6xxHkj","type":"assistant","uuid":"cdce0344-e85e-46d4-a3f3-7be49188c071","timestamp":"2026-04-27T03:12:36.607Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/hakull245/bitvector-vibe-proving","sessionId":"2b65148c-b4a0-40d0-9fba-835c4508523c","version":"2.1.120","gitBranch":"haVibeProving","slug":"hazy-chasing-owl"}
