{"parentUuid":"8d07b33a-9280-4319-8bec-a2531d3f8952","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01XSCoNQ2Z45SUfarjXAhzAf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Good point. The current wording implies `proj1`/`proj2` is always needed, but for a regular implication `H : A → B`, `apply H` works fine — the confusion only arises with `↔`. Let me sharpen it:"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":791,"cache_read_input_tokens":69899,"output_tokens":495,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":791,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":3,"output_tokens":495,"cache_read_input_tokens":69899,"cache_creation_input_tokens":791,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":791},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CaTYt5fwGc6r13R16rcd1","type":"assistant","uuid":"80a9d430-b8be-4889-a7c8-c96f55a84e35","timestamp":"2026-04-27T03:16:42.417Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/hakull245/bitvector-vibe-proving","sessionId":"2b65148c-b4a0-40d0-9fba-835c4508523c","version":"2.1.120","gitBranch":"haVibeProving","slug":"hazy-chasing-owl"}
{"parentUuid":"80a9d430-b8be-4889-a7c8-c96f55a84e35","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01XSCoNQ2Z45SUfarjXAhzAf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013BNDkMfbSFTGD6etnVRY9h","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/home/hakull245/bitvector-vibe-proving/CLAUDE.md","old_string":"**Use `proj1`/`proj2` to select iff direction — never `apply`.**\n`apply (some_iff ...)` fails when the goal or hypothesis is on the wrong side of an `↔`.\nCoq cannot auto-select the direction. Use `proj1`/`proj2` explicitly:\n\n```coq\nexact (proj1 (@bv_slt_iff_sbv2int n a b Ha Hb) H_slt).\n```","new_string":"**For `↔` lemmas, select the direction explicitly with `proj1`/`proj2`.**\n`apply` works fine for one-directional lemmas (`A → B`). But when a lemma has type `A ↔ B`,\n`apply` fails — Coq won't auto-select which direction to use. Extract the direction you need:\n\n```coq\n(* H_slt : bv_slt a b = true, goal needs (sbv2int n a < sbv2int n b)%Z *)\nexact (proj1 (@bv_slt_iff_sbv2int n a b Ha Hb) H_slt).   (* proj1 : A → B, forward *)\nexact (proj2 (@bv_slt_iff_sbv2int n a b Ha Hb) H_arith).  (* proj2 : B → A, backward *)\n```"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":791,"cache_read_input_tokens":69899,"output_tokens":495,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":791,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":3,"output_tokens":495,"cache_read_input_tokens":69899,"cache_creation_input_tokens":791,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":791},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CaTYt5fwGc6r13R16rcd1","type":"assistant","uuid":"f65e879a-ca80-41bb-84d9-3964e41821af","timestamp":"2026-04-27T03:16:46.805Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/hakull245/bitvector-vibe-proving","sessionId":"2b65148c-b4a0-40d0-9fba-835c4508523c","version":"2.1.120","gitBranch":"haVibeProving","slug":"hazy-chasing-owl"}
{"parentUuid":"f65e879a-ca80-41bb-84d9-3964e41821af","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"15159d5d-98a1-4183-b59b-c1fb5cd2bc2d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013BNDkMfbSFTGD6etnVRY9h","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /home/hakull245/bitvector-vibe-proving/CLAUDE.md has been updated successfully."}]},"uuid":"9dbd7e4d-dcad-4bb0-8037-ab3bd751768f","timestamp":"2026-04-27T03:16:46.835Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/home/hakull245/bitvector-vibe-proving/CLAUDE.md","oldString":"**Use `proj1`/`proj2` to select iff direction — never `apply`.**\n`apply (some_iff ...)` fails when the goal or hypothesis is on the wrong side of an `↔`.\nCoq cannot auto-select the direction. Use `proj1`/`proj2` explicitly:\n\n```coq\nexact (proj1 (@bv_slt_iff_sbv2int n a b Ha Hb) H_slt).\n```","newString":"**For `↔` lemmas, select the direction explicitly with `proj1`/`proj2`.**\n`apply` works fine for one-directional lemmas (`A → B`). But when a lemma has type `A ↔ B`,\n`apply` fails — Coq won't auto-select which direction to use. Extract the direction you need:\n\n```coq\n(* H_slt : bv_slt a b = true, goal needs (sbv2int n a < sbv2int n b)%Z *)\nexact (proj1 (@bv_slt_iff_sbv2int n a b Ha Hb) H_slt).   (* proj1 : A → B, forward *)\nexact (proj2 (@bv_slt_iff_sbv2int n a b Ha Hb) H_arith).  (* proj2 : B → A, backward *)\n```","originalFile":"# CLAUDE.md\n\n## Project\n\nFormally verifying cvc5's bit-vector invertibility conditions (Niemetz) in Coq 8.20.0.\nInvertibility conditions have the form `(∃x. f(x) op t) ↔ g(s, t)` over bitvectors.\n\n**Only two files matter:**\n\n- `BVList.v` — bitvector library (14k+ lines). Helper lemmas go here, added toward the end but before `End RAWBITVECTOR_LIST.`\n- `InvCond.v` — the invertibility condition proofs. All IC work goes here.\n\n## Build\n\nRun from the repo root:\n\n```bash\nmake InvCond.vo   # fast: recompile InvCond.v only\nmake              # full build\n```\n\n`_CoqProject` registers files under the `BV` namespace. Imports look like:\n\n```coq\nFrom BV Require Import BVList.\n```\n\n## Core Principle\n\n**Build incrementally, structure before solving, trust the type checker.**\nSuccess = `make InvCond.vo` passes + zero `Admitted` + no new `Axiom`s.\n\nProof workflow:\n\n1. **Structure first.** Sketch the argument with `assert`/`pose proof` before writing tactics.\n2. **Helper lemmas in BVList.v.** If an inline subproof exceeds ~20 lines, extract it there.\n3. **One `Admitted` at a time.** Fill one hole, compile, stop on error.\n4. **Reflect after each theorem.** Update CLAUDE.md with any non-obvious _patterns_ or _error fixes_.\n\n## Implicit Arguments\n\n**`BVList.v` line 33: `Set Implicit Arguments`.** All `forall (x : bitvector)` and `forall (n : N)` args are implicit — pass only proofs, bitvectors are inferred. Error symptom: `\"s\" has type \"bitvector\" while expected \"bv_sle ?a ?b = true\"`. Fix: drop the bitvector args, or prefix with `@` to make them explicit again.\n\n**Watch out for list arguments made implicit.** `list2int_geq_zero`, `list2int_lt_pow2_int`, and `bv_and_idem2` all have their list/bitvector argument implicit. When the argument can't be inferred from the goal, Coq reports \"Unable to find an instance for n\" or a type mismatch. Use `@` to pass explicitly:\n\n```coq\npose proof (@list2int_geq_zero l) as H.\npose proof (@list2int_lt_pow2_int l (length l) eq_refl) as H.\nexact (@bv_and_idem2 x s n Hx Hs).\n```\n\n## N_scope Infects Tactic Terms\n\n**`Local Open Scope N_scope` (BVList.v line 27)** means bare `-`, `+`, `*` inside tactic arguments (`replace`, `assert`, `ring`) are parsed as `N` operations — even when the values are `Z` or `nat`. Error symptom: `\"list2int t\" has type \"Z\" while it is expected to have type \"N\"`. Fix: always annotate with `%Z` or `%nat`:\n\n```coq\nreplace (a - b + c)%Z with (a - b + 1 * c)%Z by ring.\nassert (Hls : length s = 0%nat) by lia.\nreplace (length t - 1)%nat with (length s - 1)%nat in H by lia.\n```\n\n## Integer Bridges (critical for signed arithmetic)\n\n| Bridge      | Type                | Meaning                                         |\n| ----------- | ------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| `bv2nat_a`  | `bitvector → nat`   | Unsigned natural number                         |\n| `bv2int`    | `bitvector → Z`     | Unsigned Z (0..2ⁿ-1)                            |\n| `sbv2int n` | `N → bitvector → Z` | Signed two's-complement Z (-2^(n-1)..2^(n-1)-1) |\n\n`sbv2int n v = bv2int v - 2ⁿ` if MSB=1, else `bv2int v`.\n\nKey bridge lemma: `bv_slt_iff_sbv2int` — connects `bv_slt` to `<` on Z via `sbv2int`.\nFor unsigned arithmetic, prefer `bv_ult_nat` (connects `bv_ult` to `<?` on nat).\n\n## Finding Lemmas in BVList.v\n\n**NEVER `cat BVList.v` or read the full file.** It is 14,000+ lines.\n\n**Step 1 — Grep for candidate names:**\n\n```bash\ngrep -n \"Lemma\\|Theorem\" BVList.v | grep -i \"keyword\"\n```\n\n**Step 2 — Read only the relevant line range:**\nUse the line number from grep to read ~30 lines around the lemma.\n\n**Keyword index** — seed your searches with these names:\n\nOperations: `bv_and`, `bv_or`, `bv_xor`, `bv_not`, `bv_neg`, `bv_add`, `bv_subt'`,\n`bv_mult`, `bv_shl`, `bv_shr`, `bv_shl_a`, `bv_concat`\n\nComparisons: `bv_ult`, `bv_ule`, `bv_ugt`, `bv_uge`, `bv_slt`, `bv_sle`, `bv_sgt`, `bv_sge`\n\nConstants: `zeros`, `one`, `signed_min`, `signed_max`, `mk_list_false`, `mk_list_true`\n\nBridges: `bv2nat_a`, `bv2int`, `sbv2int`, `pow2_int_N`\n\nSizes: `bv_shl_size`, `bv_add_size`, `signed_min_size`, `bv_neg_size`, `bv_not_size`\n\n## Proof Tactics — General Pitfalls\n\n**Save hypotheses before `set`/`fold` chains.**\nAfter `rewrite <iff_lemma> in H` + `unfold` + `set/fold`, subterms inside `H` (e.g. sign bits)\nbecome inaccessible to further `rewrite ... in H`. Copy first:\n\n```coq\npose proof H as H_orig.          (* save original form *)\nrewrite (@some_iff ...) in H.    (* now transform H freely *)\n```\n\nThen derive sub-goals from `H_orig` using `proj1`/`proj2`.\n\n**Use `proj1`/`proj2` to select iff direction — never `apply`.**\n`apply (some_iff ...)` fails when the goal or hypothesis is on the wrong side of an `↔`.\nCoq cannot auto-select the direction. Use `proj1`/`proj2` explicitly:\n\n```coq\nexact (proj1 (@bv_slt_iff_sbv2int n a b Ha Hb) H_slt).\n```\n\n**After rewriting a goal to Z form, close with `rewrite sign. simpl. lia.`**\nOnce the goal has been converted (e.g. via `bv_slt_iff_sbv2int` + `unfold sbv2int`) to a Z\ncomparison with `if-then-else` sign branches, tactics like `bv_slt_tf` that expect a `bv_slt = true`\ngoal will fail. Rewrite the sign bits from `eqn:` hypotheses, then `simpl. lia.`:\n\n```coq\nrewrite Hsign_pos, Ht_sign_neg. simpl. lia.\n```\n\n## Checklist Before Claiming a Proof Done\n\n```bash\nmake InvCond.vo                  # must succeed\ngrep \"Admitted\" InvCond.v        # must return nothing\n```\n\n## Current Open Problem\n\nNone — `bvor_slt` was the last open theorem and is now proven.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":111,"oldLines":12,"newStart":111,"newLines":14,"lines":[" "," Then derive sub-goals from `H_orig` using `proj1`/`proj2`."," ","-**Use `proj1`/`proj2` to select iff direction — never `apply`.**","-`apply (some_iff ...)` fails when the goal or hypothesis is on the wrong side of an `↔`.","-Coq cannot auto-select the direction. Use `proj1`/`proj2` explicitly:","+**For `↔` lemmas, select the direction explicitly with `proj1`/`proj2`.**","+`apply` works fine for one-directional lemmas (`A → B`). But when a lemma has type `A ↔ B`,","+`apply` fails — Coq won't auto-select which direction to use. Extract the direction you need:"," "," ```coq","-exact (proj1 (@bv_slt_iff_sbv2int n a b Ha Hb) H_slt).","+(* H_slt : bv_slt a b = true, goal needs (sbv2int n a < sbv2int n b)%Z *)","+exact (proj1 (@bv_slt_iff_sbv2int n a b Ha Hb) H_slt).   (* proj1 : A → B, forward *)","+exact (proj2 (@bv_slt_iff_sbv2int n a b Ha Hb) H_arith).  (*